1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
y = m · x + b. Where do m, x and b come from? Nobody ever showed you.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
x is the day. That is all x ever was.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,600
A small shop. Four days of sales: 30, 40, 50, 60.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,800
m? Look at the step from one day to the next.

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,000
Ten more. Ten more. Ten more. The same jump every time: 10.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,600
Drag that 10 into m. That is m — m is the step.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,600
Join the dots: one straight line. Now run it back past day one.

8
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,600
It started at 20. Drag that into b. That is b — b is the start.

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,800
The equation is full: y = 10 · x + 20. Now put tomorrow in.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,200
Day 5. Drag the 5 into x. x becomes 5.

11
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,800
Ten times five, plus twenty. Seventy.

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,400
We learned this at school. Nobody ever said what for.

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:40,000
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
